From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:05:53 +0200
Subject: media: sun6i-csi: Take the bus width from the format when there is no
 endpoint

The interface data width comes from the source's device tree endpoint.
A pattern generator has no device tree node, so its endpoint is zero,
which falls through to the default of the switch and leaves the
interface at eight bits no matter which format is configured. Ask for a
twelve bit bayer pattern and the bus stays eight bits wide, which is
invisible from userspace: the capture succeeds and the samples come back
left justified, looking like twelve bit data that happens to have its
low four bits clear.

Carry the width each format puts on the bus in the format table, and use
it when the endpoint does not give one. Only the data width is taken
this way -- the combined-YUV decisions still key off the endpoint -- so
a source that does have a node behaves exactly as before.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
